<h1>Willie Wilson</h1>
<p>Businessman, fourth run for mayor. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>Founder of Omar Medical Supplies, former McDonald&#39;s franchisee, and producer of the gospel show Singsation; 78, a sharecropper&#39;s son from Louisiana who left school in the seventh grade. This is his fourth run for mayor, funded mostly with his own money.</p>
<p><a href="/directdemocracy/app/candidate/Mg0DTiPuSyRCjXnNjBWneSPfX5u1">Full platform, open to comments</a></p>
<p><a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website (williewilson2027.com)</a></p>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Willie Wilson for Mayor 2027</li>
<li>Raised: $404K</li>
<li>Spent: $413K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $48K</li>
<li>Since the committee formed May 19, 2026, through Sept. 30. $400,000 of the third quarter&#39;s money was loans from the candidate; the committee owes him $450,000. <a href="https://elections.il.gov/CampaignDisclosure/CommitteeDetail.aspx?id=41192" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>6% of likely voters in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 15 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>What they would do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Back the police without reservation and hold four police superintendents accountable, one per section of the city. <q>There ain&#39;t no way I&#39;m gonna abandon our police officers. Ain&#39;t no way,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/mayoral-candidate-profile-willie-wilson/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Feb. 16, 2023</a>)</li>
<li>Treats housing as a right and homeownership as the way families build wealth. <q>I view housing as a right. Homeownership is the cornerstone of wealth building.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">williewilson2027.com</a>)</li>
<li>Speaks plainly and runs as a servant of God rather than a politician. <q>I believe in Chicago and I believe you deserve a leader who wakes up every morning ready to serve.</q> (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/politics/2026/08/10/willie-wilson-announces-4th-run-for-chicago-mayor" rel="nofollow noopener">Sun-Times, Aug. 10, 2026</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>Main points</h3>
<p>Police: Full support for the police, with four superintendents, one for each section of the city, held accountable.</p>
<p>Taxes: Lower real estate taxes, treat red light cameras as a tax to get rid of, cut taxes for working people and businesses, and bring in new revenue through new businesses.</p>
<p>Housing and transit: Housing as a right with homeownership at the center, and a clean, safe, affordable CTA.</p>
<h3>Next to the others</h3>
<p>Only Wilson: Four police superintendents instead of one.</p>
<p>Taxes: Wilson, Holberg, and Kitover promise lower taxes; Giannoulias would hold the levy flat; Johnson would raise them on the ultra-rich.</p>
<p>Experience: Wilson&#39;s fourth run for mayor; Pappas, Quigley, Cardenas, and Mendoza have run citywide or countywide before.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would try to lower real estate taxes, get rid of red light cameras as a hidden tax, cut taxes for working people and businesses, and bring in revenue by attracting new businesses.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>We&#39;ll try to lower real estate taxes. The red light cameras is a form of taxes,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/mayoral-candidate-profile-willie-wilson/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Feb. 16, 2023</a>)</li>
<li><q>I think I would bring new taxes in by new businesses,</q> (<a href="https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/mayoral-candidate-profile-willie-wilson/" rel="nofollow noopener">CBS Chicago, Feb. 16, 2023</a>)</li>
<li><q>I will cut taxes for working class citizens and businesses.</q> (<a href="https://williewilson2027.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">williewilson2027.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>Produces Singsation, the first nationally syndicated Black-owned gospel TV show, and has run for president and the US Senate under his own Willie Wilson Party. (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willie_Wilson_(businessman)" rel="nofollow noopener">en.wikipedia.org</a>)</li>
</ul>
